QUESTION
Student Marks Analyser Project

**Goal:** a console program that stores student names and marks, calculates results, and prints a clean report.

**Steps**
1. Store data in arrays
2. Validate input
3. Calculate total, average, highest and lowest
4. Assign grades
5. Search a student
6. Sort results
7. Print with template literals
8. Handle missing or invalid data
9. Split logic into helper functions
10. Test with different datasets

ANSWER
let names = ["Aman", "Deepti", "Rahul"];
let marks = [80, 90, 60];

let total = 0;
let highest = marks[0];
let lowest = marks[0];

for (let i = 0; i < marks.length; i++) {
    total = total + marks[i];

    if (marks[i] > highest) {
        highest = marks[i];
    }

    if (marks[i] < lowest) {
        lowest = marks[i];
    }

    let grade;

    if (marks[i] >= 80) {
        grade = "A";
    } else if (marks[i] >= 60) {
        grade = "B";
    } else {
        grade = "C";
    }

    console.log(names[i], marks[i], grade);
}

console.log("Total:", total);
console.log("Average:", total / marks.length);
console.log("Highest:", highest);
console.log("Lowest:", lowest);
